{"foreign_part": "ἐρᾶν", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "grc", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-001", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "His power and extent is very large, and in that twofold division of Love, φιλεῖν and ἐρᾶν", "unit": "3.2.1.1"}
{"foreign_part": "ultor a tergo Deus", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-002", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "we find it true, that ultor a tergo Deus", "unit": "1.2.1.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-003", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "This they make a sport of, and will do it to their friends and confederates, against oaths, vows, promises, by treachery or otherwise", "unit": "djr"}
{"foreign_part": "Per fas & nefas", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-004", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "still seeking what sacrifice he may offer to his golden god, Per fas & nefas", "unit": "1.2.3.12"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-005", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Thus they many times wilfully pervert the good temperature of their bodies, stifle their wits, strangle nature, and degenerate into beasts.", "unit": "1.2.2.2"}
{"foreign_part": "Mare liberum", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-006", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Tush, Mare liberum", "unit": "djr"}
{"foreign_part": "sed nostra fit inertia, &c.", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-007", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Non fatigata aut effoeta humus , as Columella well informs Sylvinus, sed nostra fit inertia, &c.", "unit": "djr"}
{"foreign_part": "cum ego non summis viris comparo, sed simillimum Deo judico", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-008", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Temperance is a bridle of gold, and that can use it aright, cum ego non summis viris comparo, sed simillimum Deo judico", "unit": "2.2.1.2"}
{"foreign_part": "occidit animam", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-009", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "one saves, the other kills, occidit animam", "unit": "3.4.2.6"}
{"foreign_part": "omnes tibicines insaniunt, ubi semel efflant, avolat illico mens", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-010", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Athenaeus saith as much of Fiddlers, & musarum luscinias , Musicians, omnes tibicines insaniunt, ubi semel efflant, avolat illico mens", "unit": "djr"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-011", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "But hear the Poet’s own description of it", "unit": "3.2.2.5"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-012", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "that is rheumatic and gouty, hath some twenty diseases, perhaps but one eye, one leg, never a nose, no hair on his head, wit in his brains, nor honesty, if he have land or money, she will have him before all other suitors", "unit": "3.2.2.3"}
{"foreign_part": "ob regnum", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-013", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Charles the Great was an earnest suitor to Irene the Empress, but, saith Zonarus, ob regnum", "unit": "3.2.2.3"}
{"foreign_part": "medii inter Deos & homines", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-014", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "For so they were Semi-dii, demigods, some medii inter Deos & homines", "unit": "3.4.1.3"}
{"foreign_part": "Nemo in nostra civitate mendicus esto", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-015", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Nemo in nostra civitate mendicus esto , saith Plato, he will have them purged from a Commonwealth, as a bad humour from the body, that are like so many Ulcers and Boils, and must be cured before the Melancholy body can be eased.", "unit": "djr"}
{"foreign_part": "cum alia honesta venerem saepe exercendo", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-016", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "In some cases again, if they be much dejected and brought low in body, and now ready to despair through anguish, grief, and too sensible a feeling of their misery, a cup of wine and full diet is not amiss, and as Valescus adviseth, cum alia honesta venerem saepe exercendo", "unit": "3.2.5.1"}
{"foreign_part": "omnia perturbabant", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-017", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "If he prescribed hot medicines, they would prescribe cold, miscentes pro calidis frigida, pro frigidis humida, pro purgantibus astringentia, binders for purgatives, omnia perturbabant", "unit": "2.4.1.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-018", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "otio superstitioso seclusi", "unit": "1.2.2.6"}
{"foreign_part": "funerata est haec pars jam, quae fuit olim Achillea", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-019", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "30. 20, and now complains with him in Petronius, funerata est haec pars jam, quae fuit olim Achillea", "unit": "3.3.4.2"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-020", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "85. To these you may add, if you please, that conceited tale of a Jew, so visited in like sort, and so cured, out of Poggius Florentinus.", "unit": "1.2.2.4"}
{"foreign_part": "burras, quisquiliasque ineptiasque", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-021", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Heretofore learning was graced by judicious scholars, but now noble sciences are vilified by base and illiterate scribblers, that either write for vainglory, need, to get money, or as Parasites to flatter and collogue with some great men, they put out burras, quisquiliasque ineptiasque", "unit": "djr"}
{"foreign_part": "cui formam Paphia, & Charites tribuere decorum", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-022", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Her beauty belike, and comeliness of person, that is commonly the main object, she is a most absolute form in his eye at least, cui formam Paphia, & Charites tribuere decorum", "unit": "3.2.5.3"}
{"foreign_part": "corpus exangue pallet, corpus gracile, oculi cavi", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-023", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "deliver as much, corpus exangue pallet, corpus gracile, oculi cavi", "unit": "3.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-024", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Banishment a great misery, as Tyrtaeus describes it in an Epigram of his", "unit": "1.2.4.7"}
{"foreign_part": "licet in ludicris ludere", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-025", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Synesius approves it, licet in ludicris ludere", "unit": "3.1.1.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-026", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Look for more in Isocrates, Seneca, Plutarch, Epictetus, &c., and for defect, consult with cheese trenchers and painted cloths.", "unit": "2.3.7.1"}
{"foreign_part": "ne in posterum querantur de inanibus stupris", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-027", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "exclaims against it, and all such rash monastical vows, and would have such persons seriously to consider what they do, whom they admit, ne in posterum querantur de inanibus stupris", "unit": "3.2.5.5"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-028", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Carnificinam exercent", "unit": "3.4.1.2"}
{"foreign_part": "lethaeoque jacet condita sarcophago", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-029", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Another complains of a most sweet wife, a young wife, Nondum sustulerat flavum Proserpina crinem , such a wife as no mortal man ever had, so good a wife, but she is now dead and gone, lethaeoque jacet condita sarcophago", "unit": "2.3.5.1"}
{"foreign_part": "philosophiam Aristotelis metereologicam vehementer irrisi, cum, &c.", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-roman-before-bracket-030", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Hic ego, saith Acosta, philosophiam Aristotelis metereologicam vehementer irrisi, cum, &c.", "unit": "2.2.3.1"}
