{"gold": "la", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h-sidenote-019", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "Taxando & ab his deterrendo humanam lasciviam & insaniam, sed & remedia docendo, non igitur candidus lector nobis succenseat, &c", "unit": "3.1.1.1"}
{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h-sidenote-020", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "1 Thessal", "unit": "3.2.5.5"}
{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h-sidenote-021", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "1 cap", "unit": "2.3.4.1"}
{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h-sidenote-022", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "Hispan", "unit": "3.4.2.1"}
{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h-sidenote-023", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "Ecclus", "unit": "2.1.4.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h-sidenote-024", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "Oppressus paupertate animus nihil eximium aut sublime cogitare potest, amoenitates literarum, aut elegantiam, quoniam nihil praesidii in his ad vitae commodum videt, primo negligere, mox odisse incipit", "unit": "1.2.3.15"}
{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h-sidenote-025", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "lib", "unit": "1.4.1.1"}
{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h-sidenote-026", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "52, 55, 59, &c", "unit": "2.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h-sidenote-027", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "Adelph", "unit": "2.3.7.1"}
{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h-sidenote-028", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "3 epist", "unit": "3.2.5.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h-sidenote-029", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "Ira sine causa, velocitas irae", "unit": "1.3.1.2"}
{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h-sidenote-030", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "3 de vit", "unit": "3.2.5.2"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-verse-001", "stratum": "verse", "text": "And troubles him full sore God knows,", "unit": "argument"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h-verse-002", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Contestata suas, sed nec sibi deperiisse.", "unit": "2.2.4.1"}
{"gold": "grc", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h-verse-003", "stratum": "verse", "text": "ʼΑγαθὴ δὲ παραίφασις ἐστὶν ἑταίρου.", "unit": "2.2.6.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-verse-004", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Fairest of fair, that fairness doth excel.", "unit": "3.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h-verse-005", "stratum": "verse", "text": "——— statua taciturnius exit,", "unit": "1.2.3.15"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h-verse-006", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Non me Pelignus, nec spernet Mantua vatem,", "unit": "3.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h-verse-007", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Elige cui dicas, tu mihi sola places,", "unit": "3.2.5.5"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h-verse-008", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Vult famulis, vult etiam ancillis, & catulo meo.", "unit": "3.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h-verse-009", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Et genus aequoreum, pecudes, pictaeque volucres", "unit": "3.2.1.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h-verse-010", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Spera Batte, tibi melius lux Crastina ducet;", "unit": "2.3.3.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-english-001", "stratum": "english", "text": ", a pot-companion, by Plato’s own confession, a sturdy drinker;", "unit": "djr"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-english-002", "stratum": "english", "text": "3, assigning other causes, which are copiously censured and confuted by Aelianus Montaltus, cap.", "unit": "1.3.3.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-english-003", "stratum": "english", "text": "Zoophytes were fit to be considered in such an expedition, and amongst the rest, that of Herberstein his Tartar lamb, Hector Boethius’ goose-bearing tree in the Orcades, to which Cardan lib.", "unit": "2.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-english-004", "stratum": "english", "text": "Masinissa was married to that fair captive Sophonisba, King Syphax’s wife, the same day that he saw her first, to prevent Scipio and Laelius, lest they should determine otherwise of her.", "unit": "3.2.5.5"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-english-005", "stratum": "english", "text": "If you, what is it of which thou boastest so much?", "unit": "2.3.2.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-english-006", "stratum": "english", "text": "To open months and Haemorrhoids is very good Physic, if they have been formerly stopped.", "unit": "2.5.1.4"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-english-007", "stratum": "english", "text": "So that the hearing is as frequently deluded as the sight, from the same causes almost, as he that hears bells, will make them sound what he list.", "unit": "1.3.3.1"}
{"foreign_part": "Fortuna sua a cujusque fingitur moribus, qui cauti, prudentes, voti compotes, &c.", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h-english-008", "stratum": "english", "text": "Wisdom, diligence, discretion, may mitigate if not quite alter such decrees, Fortuna sua a cujusque fingitur moribus, qui cauti, prudentes, voti compotes, &c.", "unit": "3.2.5.5"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-english-009", "stratum": "english", "text": "But this is as clear as the Sun, and needs no further illustration.", "unit": "1.2.4.5"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h-english-010", "stratum": "english", "text": "but I should rather refer it to Madness, as most do.", "unit": "1.1.1.4"}
